WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.759
Even though we're only a few months into the
new decade, the 2020s have already been defined

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.720
by an international health crisis known as
COVID-19.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:12.100
After originating in the Wuhan province of
China, this particularly dangerous form of

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.100
coronavirus has spread throughout the world
at a much faster rate than most could have

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.539
anticipated, creating a worldwide atmosphere
of fear as a virus deadlier than the seasonal

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.820
flu strikes the most vulnerable populations.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.710
To try and prevent the incredibly rapid spread
of COVID-19, some countries are limiting travel

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.869
and closing their borders after a terrible
outbreak, Italy placed limits on all travel

00:00:31.869 --> 00:00:35.740
and put its residents under a strict quarantine,
essentially closing some of the world's most

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:41.270
historically relevant major cities and unsurprisingly,
this shutdown is also affecting the entertainment

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.380
industry in a big way.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.500
Film festivals and premieres are getting rescheduled
and canceled right and left, and between quarantined

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:51.890
shooting locations, contaminated cast and
crew members, and concerns about crowds attending

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:56.540
new movies, a lot of projects have ground
to a screeching halt in the face of COVID-19.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:02.080
One of the first cinematic casualties of COVID-19
was the final outing for Daniel Craig as James

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.860
Bond, halting one of the biggest movies of
the spring season.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:10.030
In early March of 2020, MGM, Universal, and
the producers of No Time to Die announced

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:15.260
that the film's original release of April
10, 2020 would no longer come to fruition,

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.340
and the film would instead have to wait until
November 25, 2020.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.480
"You're late."

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.840
In a statement obtained by the BBC, the producers
explained their reasoning, saying,

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.100
"Just one person, who may not even show symptoms,
could infect the rest of the audience.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:28.820
It's just a movie.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:32.820
The health and well-being of fans around the
world, and their families, is more important.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.470
We have all waited over four years for this
film.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:39.260
Another few months will not damage the quality
of the film and only help the box office for

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:40.720
Daniel Craig's final hurrah."

00:01:41.229 --> 00:01:45.500
Though some Bond fans will definitely be disappointed
by this delay, it's clear that the reasoning

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:50.180
behind the choice wasn't just sound, but extraordinarily
considerate to those most affected by this

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:50.680
virus.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.800
Certainly, Craig and crew wanted fans to see
their newest film as soon as possible, but

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.200
this humane and prescient decision will absolutely
protect people from this viral outbreak, as

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.600
well as drum up even more anticipation for
Craig's final Bond film.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.540
As COVID-19 spreads, the atmosphere surrounding
this pandemic is becoming more tense and frightening,

00:02:08.549 --> 00:02:12.950
and as such, a stark dystopian tale about
an alien apocalypse might not be a huge theatrical

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.860
success right at this exact moment.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:19.700
That might be just one reason as to why A
Quiet Place Part II, the sequel to John Krasinski's

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:24.610
directorial horror debut which premiered to
rave reviews in 2018, has been officially

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.940
placed on the backburner for the spring release
season.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.011
In a statement, Paramount announced that though
they were placing A Quiet Place Part 2 on

00:02:31.011 --> 00:02:35.010
a temporary hold, they don't yet have a new
release date for the film, which finds Emily

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:39.040
Blunt's character trying to protect her family
in a world where monsters can track your every

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:39.540
sound.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.700
Producers for the movie said in a statement,

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:46.400
"After much consideration, and in light of
the ongoing and developing situation concerning

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.670
coronavirus and restrictions on global travel
and public gatherings, Paramount Pictures

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.930
will be moving the worldwide release of A
Quiet Place Part II.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:57.840
We believe in and support the theatrical experience,
and we look forward to bringing this film

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.920
to audiences this year once we have a better
understanding of the impact of this pandemic

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.900
on the global theatrical marketplace."

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:09.700
The CW's wildest teen show is also facing
delays as a result of COVID-19, leading the

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.720
residents of Riverdale in the lurch.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:17.420
The Archie Comics adaptation, which also faced
a series of hardships in 2019 due to the unexpected

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.400
death of series star Luke Perry, was forced
to halt production as a result of possible

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.400
contamination.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:26.300
The Hollywood Reporter announced that the
Vancouver-set production put a hold on shooting

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:30.319
its upcoming fourth season, out of an abundance
of caution after someone on the show's team

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.240
may have come in contact with the virus.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.140
At the time of the announcement, the delay
was open-ended.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:39.200
Though Riverdale fans will undoubtedly be
disappointed, the health of the cast and crew

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.960
is obviously the most important consideration
for the show.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:47.500
If fans were hoping that the next Fast &amp; Furious
film would arrive on... well, a fast and furious

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.340
schedule, it looks like they'll be disappointed.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:50.720
"You think this is a joke?

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:51.940
Huh?"

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:57.120
In the wake of the COVID-19 outbreak, Fast
&amp; Furious 9 is facing a serious delay, moving

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:01.420
its release date by a full year to accommodate
audiences trying to avoid this virus.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:05.600
Universal Studios announced that the film
would be delayed nearly a full year, jumping

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.380
from May 22, 2020 to April 2, 2021.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:10.880
As the team said on Twitter,

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:15.080
"We feel all the love and the anticipation
you have for the next chapter in our saga.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:18.280
That's why it's especially tough to let you
know that we have to move the release date

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:18.780
of the film.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:22.600
It's become clear that it won't be possible
for all of our fans around the world to see

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:23.500
the film this May."

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:27.500
Though the Fast &amp; Furious crew knows their
fans are bummed, they reassured their loyal

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.180
followers that the decision was made with
safety in mind:

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.800
"While we know there is disappointment in
having to wait a little while longer, this

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:37.120
move is made with the safety of everyone as
our foremost consideration.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:40.820
Moving will allow our global family to experience
our new chapter together.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.200
We'll see you next spring."

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:46.560
Even the Marvel Cinematic Universe isn't immune
to coronavirus concerns.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:50.500
Along with several other Disney projects,
the upcoming Disney+ show The Falcon and the

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:55.100
Winter Soldier, which follows Anthony Mackie
and Sebastian Stan as Sam Wilson and Bucky

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.900
Barnes, has been delayed due to this growing
pandemic.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:02.320
Exactly what effect this will have on the
series' intended Fall 2020 premiere remains

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.080
to be seen.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.060
"That's smart.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:05.860
Good strategy."

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:10.460
The production was shut down while filming
in Prague, in the heart of the Czech Republic.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:15.030
Stan took to Instagram to address Marvel fans,
lavishing praise upon Prague and the production

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.320
itself with the caption,

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:16.820
"Prague.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:17.540
What a city.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.180
We've been shooting TheFalconAndTheWinterSoldier
and experiencing one of the most beautiful

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:24.420
cities in the world filled with the most wonderful
and welcoming people.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.120
Now we are being sent home.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:26.760
Too soon.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:29.520
Prague, you're gonna be in my thoughts for
a long time.

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:30.280
Thank you.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:30.900
Will be back.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:31.580
Thinking of you."

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:36.920
These two superheroes might be unstoppable
in the MCU, but COVID-19 has put their story

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.160
into cryo-freeze for now.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:43.230
In the midst of a frightening pandemic, audiences
are looking for escapist fare more than ever,

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:46.870
but unfortunately, some upcoming romantic
comedies are getting shelved until further

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:48.220
notice due to the virus.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:53.940
One such casualty is The Lovebirds, Paramount's
upcoming rom-com starring Issa Rae and Kumail

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.540
Nanjiani, which has been pulled from the studio's
lineup.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:06:01.320
Ahead of its planned April 3, 2020 release,
the Michael Showalter film has been placed

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:05.060
on an indefinite hold, with no new release
date announced just yet.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:09.780
Fans of animated Disney classics — and their
live-action remakes — were surely disappointed

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:14.050
when the studio announced that their highly
anticipated live-action reboot of Mulan would

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:16.460
also face delays due to the coronavirus crisis.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:21.180
Before the film's planned release on March
27, Disney broke the news that Mulan would

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.410
simply have to wait.

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:23.540
"It is decided.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:25.940
Come and sit down."

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:31.280
Per Niki Caro, the film's director, the decision
was made out of respect to the global pandemic,

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:35.240
and she took to Instagram to explain the film's
unfortunate delay, writing, in part,

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:39.320
"We are so excited to share this film with
the world, but given the current ever-shifting

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:44.289
circumstances we are all experiencing, unfortunately,
we have to postpone the worldwide release

00:06:44.289 --> 00:06:45.280
of MULAN for now.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.300
Our hearts are with everyone the world over
who is affected by this virus, and we hope

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:53.259
that Mulan's fighting spirit will continue
to inspire those who are working so hard to

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.080
keep us all safe.”

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.720
Currently, there's no new release date set
just yet for Mulan.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:03.039
Sometimes, when a film faces delay after delay
after delay, it seems like it might never

00:07:03.039 --> 00:07:07.039
see the light of day; unfortunately, that
seems to be the case for the X-Men spin-off

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:07.940
The New Mutants.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.980
After facing multiple delays due to a number
of factors, including Fox's acquisition by

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:17.069
Disney, and rumors of reshoots that apparently
didn't even end up happening, The New Mutants

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:20.700
has been delayed yet again thanks to the ongoing
threat of coronavirus.

00:07:21.069 --> 00:07:24.760
This news comes after questions over whether
or not Disney would even release the film,

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:28.699
which was one of the holdovers from Fox's
theatrical schedule, but it ended up with

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:30.180
an April 3rd release date...

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:31.200
“Not anymore.”

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:35.700
… only to be pulled yet again, with no new
release date as of the making of this video.

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:40.360
Smaller films are likely to take an even bigger
hit when it comes to delayed releases.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:45.020
Antlers, a daring indie horror film starring
Keri Russell and Jesse Plemons, is just one

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:45.520
example.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:50.580
With a planned April 17th release by Searchlight
Pictures, Antlers, which is directed by Crazy

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:55.060
Heart helmer Scott Cooper and produced by
horror auteur Guillermo del Toro, has been

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.759
delayed by parent company Disney.

00:07:56.759 --> 00:08:01.669
Like some of Disney's other delays, including
the much pricier Mulan and The New Mutants,

00:08:01.669 --> 00:08:04.840
Antlers also has no planned release date as
of the making of this video.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:10.040
The coronavirus-related delays and cancellations
are coming out of Hollywood at a fast and

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:12.180
furious pace, indeed, per Variety.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:17.420
As of the making of this video, you can add
CBS reality TV staples Survivor and Amazing

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:18.480
Race to the list.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:22.160
Both shows have temporarily shut down production
on their current seasons.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:26.220
Season 2 production of Apple’s The Morning
Show, starring Reese Witherspoon and Jennifer

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.560
Aniston, is also going on a two-week hiatus,
effective immediately.

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:34.320
Long-running hospital drama Grey’s Anatomy
is also getting delayed, but the diagnosis

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.020
isn’t too dire.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:39.800
The current season is basically in the can,
with 21 out of a planned 25 episodes filmed.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:44.169
Out of an abundance of caution, however, the
showrunners have halted production “for

00:08:44.169 --> 00:08:46.340
at least two weeks” in response to the virus.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:50.630
As for films, production on the Baz Lurhmann
directed “Untitled Elvis Project“ has

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:55.339
been halted, along with the highly anticipated
Mission Impossible: 7 with Tom Cruise and

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:59.560
the comedy Official Competition, starring
Penelope Cruz and Antonio Banderas.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:04.459
And sorry, kids: the release of Sony’s Peter
Rabbit 2 has been pushed back from late March/early

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.360
April to August 2020.

